<div class="localcard"><div><p class="kicker">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>Hail</li><li>Wind</li><li>Tornadoes</li><li>Frozen pipes</li><li>Fire</li></ul></div><dl><div><dt>Housing mix</dt><dd>Large historic homes near downtown and Heartwell Park, brick commercial buildings, mid-century ranches, farms</dd></div><div><dt>Storm history</dt><dd>Frequent south-central hail and severe wind</dd></div></dl></div>

<h2>Historic homes and a brick downtown</h2>
<p>Hastings, the birthplace of Kool-Aid, has a downtown of brick commercial buildings and neighborhoods of large older homes, especially around Heartwell Park and near Hastings College. Wood siding, porches, tall windows and steep roofs are common. Those features take more time and different materials to repair than a typical newer house.</p>
<h2>Weather in south-central Nebraska</h2>
<p>Severe thunderstorms bring hail and damaging winds across Adams County most years. Older roofs, metal outbuildings and mature trees all contribute to claims.</p>
<h2>What we see in Hastings</h2>
<ul>
<li>Wood siding and trim priced as vinyl replacement</li>
<li>Steep roofs and porch roofs missing from the scope</li>
<li>Brick commercial buildings with flat roof systems</li>
<li>Farm outbuildings with hail-dented steel</li>
</ul>
<h2>Serving Adams County</h2>
<p>We work in Hastings, Juniata, Kenesaw and the surrounding rural areas.</p>

